> In fact, R_DOC_DIR is set in /usr/bin/R.

R_DOC_DIR is set by the shell script wrapper for R, and starting an 
embedded R is done without those variables set. There seems to be 
something for the rpy2.rinterface level (to make it easier to 
configure), and set by default at the rpy2.robjects level.

Yet, interestingly help.start() seems to work without tweaking any 
variable here.

> Is there any way I can access these environment variables from within
